WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:03.053
Welcome to Growth in Portfolio Tracker.

2
00:00:03.053 --> 00:00:06.456
This workspace answers three related but different questions.

3
00:00:06.456 --> 00:00:11.562
Dollars shows what the account is worth and how its value changed.

4
00:00:11.562 --> 00:00:16.667
Vs market compares the selected holdings with a benchmark using transaction-aware returns.

5
00:00:16.667 --> 00:00:23.475
Lots separates the results that are still open from gains and losses that were already realized.

6
00:00:23.475 --> 00:00:33.260
In this walkthrough, we will explain every tab, the summary bubbles, and the charts that turn account history into a clear performance story.

7
00:00:34.460 --> 00:00:37.417
Start with the controls at the top.

8
00:00:37.417 --> 00:00:44.176
Dollars, Vs market, and Lots are three views of the same selected account and performance range.

9
00:00:44.176 --> 00:00:50.090
The date presets run from one day through five years, All, Life, and Custom.

10
00:00:50.090 --> 00:00:54.315
Except for Life, returns end at the latest market observation.

11
00:00:54.315 --> 00:01:00.229
Life is different: it is cost-basis gain and loss rather than a market-return window.

12
00:01:00.229 --> 00:01:12.480
With the same account, holdings scope, and date range, Tracker Total Return percent is designed to reconcile across Growth, Total Return, Dashboard, and Gains and Losses after the close.

13
00:01:13.680 --> 00:01:16.874
The Dollars tab begins with the account-level bubbles.

14
00:01:16.874 --> 00:01:23.661
Start Value and End Value are the account values at the two ends of the selected window.

15
00:01:23.661 --> 00:01:29.650
They include tracked cash, and the account reading can also include open-option value when shown.

16
00:01:29.650 --> 00:01:32.045
Tracker Total Return dollars is different.

17
00:01:32.045 --> 00:01:39.631
It is the cash-flow-adjusted investment result: price return plus distributions, without treating deposits, purchases, or sales as investment gain.

18
00:01:39.631 --> 00:01:50.810
Tracker Total Return percent expresses that same return as a percentage, making it the best number to compare with the other Growth tabs and the Total Return screen.

19
00:01:52.010 --> 00:01:56.632
Below the bubbles, Portfolio Value plots the account over time.

20
00:01:56.632 --> 00:02:03.104
The portfolio line follows recorded value, while the optional invested line provides cost-basis context.

21
00:02:03.104 --> 00:02:09.575
It is an account-value chart, so deposits, withdrawals, cash, and purchases can move it.

22
00:02:09.575 --> 00:02:13.736
The Transaction-Aware Return chart answers a cleaner investment question.

23
00:02:13.736 --> 00:02:16.971
Its price-return line shows market movement only.

24
00:02:16.971 --> 00:02:25.292
Its distributions line records income, and the tracker-total line combines the two without counting cash flows as performance.

25
00:02:25.292 --> 00:02:33.150
Toggle between return percent and amount when you want a normalized rate or the matching dollar result.

26
00:02:34.350 --> 00:02:44.204
Choose Vs market when the question is not only how much you made, but how the selected holdings performed against a benchmark.

27
00:02:44.204 --> 00:02:50.027
Enter a market ticker, such as SPY, and use Go to load it.

28
00:02:50.027 --> 00:02:59.434
The portfolio calculation does not change when you change the benchmark; only the comparison series, difference, and benchmark risk statistics change.

29
00:02:59.434 --> 00:03:10.632
The bubbles show Portfolio Grade, transaction-aware price return, open-lots price return, open-lots total return, tracker total return, and both portfolio and benchmark Sharpe and Sortino.

30
00:03:10.632 --> 00:03:13.767
Open-lots metrics include only positions still held.

31
00:03:13.767 --> 00:03:19.590
Tracker metrics also include positions that were fully closed during the selected range.

32
00:03:20.790 --> 00:03:24.454
The two index charts make the comparison visual.

33
00:03:24.454 --> 00:03:27.201
Both series begin at one hundred.

34
00:03:27.201 --> 00:03:34.987
An ending value of one hundred and fifteen means a fifteen-percent return, not a one-hundred-and-fifteen-dollar account balance.

35
00:03:34.987 --> 00:03:45.062
The Transaction-Aware Price Return Index uses market-price movement only, with the portfolio in cyan and the benchmark as the dotted orange line.

36
00:03:45.062 --> 00:03:53.763
The Transaction-Aware Total Return Index uses the same starting point but reinvests distributions, shown by the green portfolio line.

37
00:03:53.763 --> 00:04:01.090
The distance between the price and total-return readings highlights the contribution from dividends and other distributions.

38
00:04:02.290 --> 00:04:08.998
Performance by Ticker ranks the included holdings by transaction-aware total return for the selected period.

39
00:04:08.998 --> 00:04:13.023
Green bars are positive and red bars are negative.

40
00:04:13.023 --> 00:04:21.520
A long bar identifies a large percentage move, but not necessarily the largest dollar contribution, because position sizes differ.

41
00:04:21.520 --> 00:04:24.650
The Portfolio Growth Map completes that picture.

42
00:04:24.650 --> 00:04:26.886
Each tile is a holding.

43
00:04:26.886 --> 00:04:39.408
Its area reflects the holding's current tracked market value, while its color reflects its total return: red for a loss, neutral near zero, and green for a gain.

44
00:04:39.408 --> 00:04:43.880
Together, the bars and map expose both performance and concentration.

45
00:04:45.080 --> 00:04:52.539
The Lots tab, labeled Gains and Losses inside the panel, separates a selected-period replay from lifetime accounting.

46
00:04:52.539 --> 00:05:02.193
The upper bubbles follow the shared performance range: Start Value, End Value, price return, distributions, tracker total return, and their open-lot counterparts.

47
00:05:02.193 --> 00:05:06.581
Purchases and sales change weights without being counted as returns.

48
00:05:06.581 --> 00:05:12.724
The Lifetime Cost-Basis section below does not change when you move the date filter.

49
00:05:12.724 --> 00:05:28.520
It compares current value with what was paid for the shares, includes realized results for sold shares, and can show Account Value separately when cash and open option contracts need to be reconciled with a broker.

50
00:05:29.720 --> 00:05:33.899
The Lots tables bring the accounting down to each ticker.

51
00:05:33.899 --> 00:05:43.092
Unrealized lists the shares still held, with invested amount, current value, price gain or loss, dividends received, and total gain or loss.

52
00:05:43.092 --> 00:05:47.689
Realized lists closed sales, including their locked-in proceeds versus cost basis.

53
00:05:47.689 --> 00:05:57.301
Combined places both sides together for every ticker you have owned, so a fully sold position does not disappear from the lifetime picture.

54
00:05:57.301 --> 00:06:09.420
The chart above the tables compares price gain and loss with total gain and loss over time, while the ticker bars make the dividend contribution visible beside price-only results.

55
00:06:09.420 --> 00:06:15.270
Use the table tabs and Columns control to focus on the detail you need.

56
00:06:16.470 --> 00:06:21.723
To recap, use Dollars to understand account value and transaction-aware dollar return.

57
00:06:21.723 --> 00:06:32.228
Use Vs market to compare the selected holdings with a benchmark, then use its bubbles, indexes, bars, and growth map to find the drivers.

58
00:06:32.228 --> 00:06:40.545
Use Lots when you need to separate current holdings from completed sales and inspect cost-basis accounting ticker by ticker.

59
00:06:40.545 --> 00:06:46.236
Keep the account, filter, and shared date range aligned when you compare screens.

60
00:06:46.236 --> 00:06:47.987
